{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305629-wu-nung-craft-any-source","id":1305629,"title":"Wu Nung Craft? Any Source?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-17T20:40:09-07:00","id":1305629,"title":"Wu Nung Craft? Any Source?","content":"In the Mind's Eye Theatre book &quot;Laws of Ascension Companion&quot; there is a craft called the Wu Nung. They are a group formed by the traitors of the Wu Keng - this is the betrayal that their demonic overlords wish to see punished. However, I can't find any reference to the Wu Nung in the Crafts book, the Ascension Storyteller books, or anywhere, not even in Dragons to the East. Have I missed it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T20:46:45-07:00","id":1305632,"title":"","content":"I think they were invented entirely for MET.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T23:52:58-07:00","id":1305651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305629-wu-nung-craft-any-source?p=1305632#post1305632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they were invented entirely for MET.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely; they likely originate from Dragons of the East, which features the Wu-Keng elders reviving the original tradition (small t) of peasant sorcery. Endless's problem might be that he was looking specifically for the Wu Nung name, which <i>is</i> an MET original; according to the Wu-Kung lexicon in Dragons of the East, peasant magicians who aren't part of the Wu-Keng are known as the Wu.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T02:30:33-07:00","id":1305672,"title":"","content":"Marin is correct. Dragons of the East gave the Wu Keng and their non-infernal counterparts mostly equal examination (it helped that they shared some aspects of Practice, even if they do it for vastly different ends). The issue is that the book only ever called them &quot;the Shamans&quot;. It's only in MET that they were given their own name. Which was probably for the best, all things considered. The Wu Keng have always been, to put it lightly, problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T07:15:08-07:00","id":1306522,"title":"","content":"There's a reason why M20 described them as a Craft that has been wiped out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T09:33:57-07:00","id":1306546,"title":"","content":"I vaguely recall reading the name in reference to Chinese peasant magicians before. That means it probably appeared in the Book of Crafts, I've not followed Mage through its more recent editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T13:55:46-07:00","id":1306632,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, Wu Nung means &quot;peasant witch/shaman&quot;, so it could very well be a name the Wu Lung gave them (similar to the Hermetics and &quot;Hedge Wizards&quot;) rather than what they actually call themselves. Similar to how Wu Keng means &quot;pit witch&quot; more or less. (For a few years, I've started to doubt if Wu Lung is even what the Dragons properly refer to themselves as.)<br /> <br /> Wu Nung might be Jingshen Men (spirit gates); Wu Keng as Bianzhi Mingyun (weavers of fate); Wu Lung as Diguo Wushi Bu (Imperial Ministry of Wizards)? Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T21:44:19-07:00","id":1306750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305629-wu-nung-craft-any-source?p=1306632#post1306632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, Wu Nung means &quot;peasant witch/shaman&quot;, so it could very well be a name the Wu Lung gave them (similar to the Hermetics and &quot;Hedge Wizards&quot;) rather than what they actually call themselves. Similar to how Wu Keng means &quot;pit witch&quot; more or less. (For a few years, I've started to doubt if Wu Lung is even what the Dragons properly refer to themselves as.)<br /> <br /> Wu Nung might be Jingshen Men (spirit gates); Wu Keng as Bianzhi Mingyun (weavers of fate); Wu Lung as Diguo Wushi Bu (Imperial Ministry of Wizards)? Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like those titles and ideas and may use them in the future, if you don't mind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:05:45-07:00","id":1306906,"title":"","content":"Sure. Just keep in mind that it's Google Translate Chinese, so is probably a little wonky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T11:27:40-07:00","id":1306915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305629-wu-nung-craft-any-source?p=1306906#post1306906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, Wu Nung means &quot;peasant witch/shaman&quot;, so it could very well be a name the Wu Lung gave them (similar to the Hermetics and &quot;Hedge Wizards&quot;) rather than what they actually call themselves. Similar to how Wu Keng means &quot;pit witch&quot; more or less. (For a few years, I've started to doubt if Wu Lung is even what the Dragons properly refer to themselves as.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest I'm a native Chinese, and I will tell you this is relevant to Chinese.<br /> <br /> Wu Nung=\u5deb\u519c=Peasant Witch<br /> Wu Kung=\u5deb\u5751(\u5764?)=Pit Witch (This sounds strange in Chinese... )<br /> Wu Lung=\u5deb\u9f99=Dragon Witch(We Chinese usually use this translation)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305629-wu-nung-craft-any-source?p=1306906#post1306906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wu Nung might be Jingshen Men (spirit gates); Wu Keng as Bianzhi Mingyun (weavers of fate); Wu Lung as Diguo Wushi Bu (Imperial Ministry of Wizards)? Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>these thoughts...Interesting...How do you think of them?<br /> <br /> Jingshen Men=\u7cbe\u795e\u4eec\uff08\u95e8\uff1f\uff09=Spirits (Spirits' Gate?)<br /> Bianzhi Mingyun=\u7f16\u7ec7\u547d\u8fd0=Weaving Fates<br /> Diguo Wushi Bu=\u5e1d\u56fd\u5deb\u5e08\u90e8=Wizards' Ministry of Imperial <br /> <br /> Uh, but in fact WW's eastern settings are always ridiculous(at least to us Chinese). Filled with stereotypes and strange things and spelling mistakes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-24-2019, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T14:04:47-07:00","id":1306971,"title":"","content":"Chinese is somewhat difficult to translate into English, as the accepted rules for spelling, pronunciation, and such have changed and updated repeatedly over the past century, which only compounds the usual translation issues of homophones, verb tenses, plural nouns, and all the other grammar traps. Plus phrases and word usage that make no sense outside of cultural context. (Seriously, try translating the lyrics to NWA's &quot;Straight Outta Compton&quot; into any other language.) On top of this, up until about 50 years ago, when most of the English speaking world mentioned the &quot;Chinese&quot; language, they were thinking primarily about the Cantonese dialect, as it was the most used by immigrants, as well as by the film industries in Hong Kong and Taiwan. Professional interpreters make good money for a reason.<br /> <br /> Most modern stereotypes tend to come from mass media (both entertainment and news), and cut both ways. I'm in my 40s, and like most Americans my age, my initial exposure to China was imported martial arts films that ran on UHF tv on weekends, later supplemented by the Hong Kong action films that showed up in video rental outlets in the 90s. But on the other hand, I used to know a guy my age from Nigeria who told me he thought everything in America was like Miami Vice and the A-Team until his family immigrated to Milwaukee when he was 15.<br /> <br /> I think the single biggest problem with Kindred of the East is that it often acted like nothing had changed culturally in China since the 1920s - or in some cases the 1320s. There was very little about young modern urban Chinese people and how they reacted to be undead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:01:20-07:00","id":1307509,"title":"","content":"To be honest, CWoD Eastern settings, not only KotE, are almost ridiculous to all of us, yes, every native chinese gamers I meet. 20 Anniversary may be better.<br /> <br /> First WW lexicon usually combine many kinds of Pinyin(Cantonese, Madarin, W-G), we usually met big trouble when we translated them(Oh yeah...Chinese has difficulty translating Enginese) <br /> <br /> About stereotypes you mentions a lot. And some of them are strange. For example, KotE is linked a lot to Buddhism, but in fact we seldom belief it unless you has demand...Even Confuciusm reminds us more. <br /> <br /> And in my memory, whole WW eastern settings have many things to do with Hindu culture or Buddhism, but, uh, at least us Chinese youth don't have much interest in it. But many settings refer to Chinese. <br /> <br /> We can't recognize any &quot;historical&quot; figures except Qinshihuangdi... <br /> <br /> Many things in eastern settings are... very strange. I remember there is a title called &quot;Daloulaoshi(\u5927\u697c\u8001\u5e08)&quot; in Akashic Broherhood, oh what's this I talked to my friend, &quot;teachers of big building?&quot; <br /> <br /> Yes, cultural problems are always problems.Now we Chinese young people are almost modernized, traditional things do remain but it ranks second. We also think undead is cool. <br /> <br /> PS1: I can bet that I have met the most famous native Chinese gamers of WoD, because WoD is very very very obscure in China, many people will play much more famous games which like DnD or CoC or other Japanese TRPGs. But VtM basic settings(Caine, Clans, Titles) are very popular among us. <br /> <br /> And I guess many people will say MtA is a copy of Japanese Typemoon if we commendend it(Of course this should be reversed, Typemoon is a copy of MtA)<br /> <br /> PS2: I remember KotE has been covered in V5? That's a good news...After all all KotE is just a sourceseries of VtM...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-24-2019, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:10:24-07:00","id":1307514,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the supernatural don\u2019t have to reflect a mortal culture\u2019s dominate belief system. Just look at Werewolf the Apocalypse!<br /> <br /> Not disagreeing there\u2019s a lot of Orientalism in CWoD portrayal of East Asia. But I don\u2019t think \u201cthis draws too much on Buddhism for its mythology when that isn\u2019t actually our dominant belief system\u201d is inherently a problem in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:25:30-07:00","id":1307520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305629-wu-nung-craft-any-source?p=1307514#post1307514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the supernatural don\u2019t have to reflect a mortal culture\u2019s dominate belief system. Just look at Werewolf the Apocalypse!<br /> <br /> Not disagreeing there\u2019s a lot of Orientalism in CWoD portrayal of East Asia. But I don\u2019t think \u201cthis draws too much on Buddhism for its mythology when that isn\u2019t actually our dominant belief system\u201d is inherently a problem in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I just talk about our thoughts to these settings. I know this is a little unfair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T15:50:45-07:00","id":1309307,"title":"","content":"I have recently read The day of the Judgement, the last novel of the old world of darkness (not a master piece, precisely) before White wolf closed the line and I became surprised about one of the characters, Ming Xian, of the Wu keng, a renegade transsexual necromancer from a craft of evil, transsexual, necromancers, infernalists and chinese supremacist, the Wu keng. I can understand why there are not Wu keng in M20, given the political polemics of the last years in WW. Certainly, is a craft with lot of delicate themes, that have become more uncomfortable in the last years. But... what about the Wu keng? Could be the Wu nung the light version of this bunch of involuntary villains?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T19:19:50-07:00","id":1309352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305629-wu-nung-craft-any-source?p=1309307#post1309307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have recently read The day of the Judgement, the last novel of the old world of darkness (not a master piece, precisely) before White wolf closed the line and I became surprised about one of the characters, Ming Xian, of the Wu keng, a renegade transsexual necromancer from a craft of evil, transsexual, necromancers, infernalists and chinese supremacist, the Wu keng. I can understand why there are not Wu keng in M20, given the political polemics of the last years in WW. Certainly, is a craft with lot of delicate themes, that have become more uncomfortable in the last years. But... what about the Wu keng? Could be the Wu nung the light version of this bunch of involuntary villains?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, but not in the sense that they're a &quot;lighter, less offensive version of villainy&quot;... the Wu Nung are the anti-Wu Keng.<br /> <br /> The Wu Keng were around since 2nd edition, IIRC (whenever Book of Crafts came out). To summarize, they were wizards in ancient China who got all but wiped out. They made a deal with demonic entities (that they either didn't know or were in denial about the nature of), who promised them their power back in a few millennia in exchange for service. They made the mages and their heirs down the lines more or less mortgage their souls and/or avatars to them, and also imposed many restrictions - among them, forcing them to be their &quot;brides&quot; and dress and live as women (and traditional Chinese brides, to boot). They warred with the Wu Lung and carried out their &quot;husbands'&quot; will, anticipating the end of their contract in 2000.<br /> <br /> In 1999, the demons declared that the six eldest had betrayed them, added an extra 1,000 years to the contract, and refused to allow any others to be trained until the six Chou An were brought down.<br /> <br /> This may or may not have actually been the truth, but at some point, they did betray their demonic masters in training others in a different form of shamanic and demon slaying Magick (which was based on the Spirit sphere, normally banned to the Wu Keng), which may have been the original paradigm of their culture before being corrupted. In the tabletop, these demon slayers were nameless; as was pointed out before, though, the LARP called them the Wu Nung.<br /> <br /> Their magicks focus on destroying demons and dealing with evil spirits - in other words, they are a counter movement to the Wu Keng, though they are fairly new and young (or were at the turn of the century) due to having only just arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T02:22:05-07:00","id":1309393,"title":"","content":"I know that Wu Nung are not villains or infernalist, but my questions was more about the transsexualism of this craft. May be, the Wu nung are the way to discharge this group for being associated to evil magics and evil characters, etc. Does the Wu nung continue to being transexualist shamans?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T16:13:58-07:00","id":1309534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305629-wu-nung-craft-any-source?p=1309393#post1309393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that Wu Nung are not villains or infernalist, but my questions was more about the transsexualism of this craft. May be, the Wu nung are the way to discharge this group for being associated to evil magics and evil characters, etc. Does the Wu nung continue to being transexualist shamans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not any more than literally any other Mage group. My reading of Dragons of the East did not give me the impression that the Wu Nung held any particular regard for transexuality. They were just regular people, trained in the Old Ways of Chinese peasant magic, from before the Wu Keng made their infernal deal. Heck, even the Wu Keng didn't have that cross-dressing aspect at first, but had it imposed upon them a little after their pact was forged. The Wu Keng needed protection from persecution, and so their demonic masters had them go in women's clothing.<br /> <br /> I mean, a Wu Nung <i>could</i> be trans, obviously, but nothing about their Craft mandates it. It's an individual thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T19:31:08-07:00","id":1309561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1305629-wu-nung-craft-any-source?p=1309534#post1309534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not any more than literally any other Mage group. My reading of Dragons of the East did not give me the impression that the Wu Nung held any particular regard for transexuality. They were just regular people, trained in the Old Ways of Chinese peasant magic, from before the Wu Keng made their infernal deal. Heck, even the Wu Keng didn't have that cross-dressing aspect at first, but had it imposed upon them a little after their pact was forged. The Wu Keng needed protection from persecution, and so their demonic masters had them go in women's clothing.<br /> <br /> I mean, a Wu Nung <i>could</i> be trans, obviously, but nothing about their Craft mandates it. It's an individual thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. The Wu Keng are the only Craft that integrates any form of transsexuality into its identity and/or practices, which is one of the reasons it's so problematic. And the reason for it isn't rooted in THEIR own historic tradition that they're trying to preserve, or necessarily part of the members individual identity - it's part of their deal with the Feng Tu, meant to debase and humiliate the mage and mystically make them &quot;weaker&quot; and &quot;subservient&quot; to their patrons.<br /> <br /> The Wu Nung were trained with the old traditions and magic. Nothing about the tradition requires them to live as or act as a member of a different gender. They may anyways, but that's their choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}